    <tags>korean ime hangul hotkey shift-space keyboard lightweight portable</tags>
    <summary>Ultra-lightweight Shift+Space Korean/English IME toggle for Windows (5KB)</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[
**nShiftSpace** (Nexa ShiftSpace) is an ultra-lightweight Windows tray utility
that toggles the Korean/English IME with **Shift+Space** — the classic Korean
keyboard layout behavior.

- Single ~5KB executable, no C runtime, pure Win32 API
- Zero CPU while idle (uses `RegisterHotKey`, no keyboard hook)
- About 0.3MB in Task Manager (working set trimmed after startup)
- Tray menu: "Start at login" toggle (HKCU Run value, written only when you turn it on) and Exit
- Single-instance guard, tray icon auto-restore after explorer.exe restart
- Free and open source (MIT)

A keyboard-LED variant (tray icon lights up while any key is held) is available as a
separate zip on the GitHub Releases page; this package installs the standard build.
]]></description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/SosomLab/nexa-shortcut/releases</releaseNotes>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
  </files>
</package>
